---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import {
	COOKIES_PATH,
	HELP_PATH,
	LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL,
	LICENSE_PATH,
	PRIVACY_PATH,
	REFUNDS_PATH,
	SITE_BRAND,
	TERMS_PATH,
} from '../../lib/seo';
---

<LegalLayout
	title="About"
	description="About iStockVisual.com: a royalty-free visual library plus on-device studio tools for search, download, and everyday production."
	heading="About iStockVisual"
	lede="iStockVisual.com is a live stock-visual library and a small studio that runs in the browser. Search, download, and remix — without sending your own files to our servers unless you use visual search."
>
	<h2>1. What we publish</h2>
	<p>
		{SITE_BRAND} is a catalog of photos, illustrations, vectors, and 3D stills built for campaigns,
		product pages, presentations, and social posts. Listings are organized by media type (for
		example Photos), by topical category, and by the visible subject of each image. You can open a
		detail page for every asset: preview, color palette, generation prompt, similar images, and a
		download panel with size and format options.
	</p>
	<p>
		Most Library Content is generated or prepared specifically for this site. Files are released
		under a <a href={LICENSE_PATH}>CC0 License</a>. The same terms apply to every size: commercial
		and personal use are allowed, and attribution is not required. Optional credit equivalent to
		<strong> Generated by {SITE_BRAND}</strong> is welcome when the medium allows it.
	</p>

	<h2>2. How search and browsing work</h2>
	<p>
		Type a query, follow related keywords, or browse categories. Filters include orientation, colors
		matched to each image’s palette, excluded keywords, and sort order. Empty or thin result pages
		may be withheld from search engines; the public sitemap lists published asset pages, category
		hubs, tools, and core site pages.
	</p>
	<p>
		<strong>Visual search</strong> lets you drop or pick a query photo. We upload that photo only to
		match it against the library (including color). Query photos are stored briefly and deleted
		after about one hour. They are not added to the public catalog. Details are in the
		<a href={PRIVACY_PATH}>Privacy Policy</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>3. Downloads</h2>
	<p>
		Every asset can be taken as JPG, PNG, WEBP, or SVG. Free members — including visitors with no
		account — can take <strong>512</strong> and <strong>1K</strong> (1024 on the long edge).
		<strong>2K</strong>, <strong>4K</strong>, and <strong>8K</strong> need an active Pro plan or
		short pass. Filenames use the asset title, not a random code.
	</p>
	<p>
		On the detail page you can also open the on-page editor (adjust, crop and flip, remove
		background, expand). Expand on library files is a Pro feature. Free editor exports stay on the
		512 / 1K long-edge caps; Pro can work at the larger download tiers. Watermarks on the on-site
		preview are there to protect the catalog; they are not part of a completed download.
	</p>
	<p>
		Paid HD downloads follow a fair-use rule: the first 100 high-resolution (2K / 4K / 8K) files
		each day are unrestricted; after that, 10 HD downloads per hour. Plans, trials, and refunds are
		on <a href="/price">Pricing</a>, the <a href={TERMS_PATH}>Terms of Use</a>, and the
		<a href={REFUNDS_PATH}>Refund Policy</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>4. In-browser studio</h2>
	<p>
		The Tools section is a local workshop. Files you choose from your computer stay in this tab
		unless a feature clearly uploads them (visual search is the exception). The public tools are:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<a href="/tools/image">Image Editor</a> — adjust, crop, remove background, and expand
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="/tools/convert">Image Convert</a> — batch format, resize, and compress (including HEIC)
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="/tools/vectorize">Image Vectorizer</a> — bitmap to SVG with color and path controls
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="/tools/social">Social Resizer</a> — Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, Facebook, and LinkedIn frames
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="/tools/watermark">Batch Watermark</a> — text or logo marks that scale with the long edge
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="/tools/palette">Palette Generator</a> — extract swatches, copy HEX/RGB/HSL, export CSS or Tailwind
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		If you start from Library Content, the Content License and attribution still apply to that
		content and to recognizable derivatives. Outputs from your own photos remain yours.
	</p>

	<h2>5. Accounts and hosting</h2>
	<p>
		Email-and-password accounts are optional for free 512 / 1K downloads and required for Pro
		sizes. We host on Cloudflare. Account records live in Cloudflare D1. Library files and brief
		visual-search uploads live in Cloudflare R2. Theme preference stays in your browser. See the
		<a href={COOKIES_PATH}>Cookie Policy</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>6. Support</h2>
	<p>
		The <a href={HELP_PATH}>Help</a> page has an on-site assistant for license, plans, tools, and
		privacy questions. For refunds or account issues, email
		<a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>
